msgid "**Group revocation is not reliable, in both directions.** Open WebUI removes a user from a synced group only while the groups claim is non-empty, so a user who loses their last role keeps stale membership until a later login carries a non-empty claim. Conversely, a non-empty claim removes the user from *every* local group the claim does not name, including groups an administrator created by hand. Reconciling either from the deploy would mean a second writer for group membership, competing with the login-time sync and able to evict accounts the platform's own user list does not know about, so both are left to an external reconciler or an upstream fix."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Group revocation is not reliable, in both directions.** Open WebUI removes a user from a synced group only while the groups claim is non-empty, so a user who loses their last role keeps stale membership until a later login carries a non-empty claim. Conversely, a non-empty claim removes the user from *every* local group the claim does not name, including groups an administrator created by hand. Reconciling either from the deploy would mean a second writer for group membership, competing with the login-time sync and able to evict accounts the platform’s own user list does not know about, so both are left to an external reconciler or an upstream fix."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Group-Based Admin Roles:** [`files/php/oidc/client.php`](./files/php/oidc/client.php) keeps two AdminOpenAuth role-assignment rules whose ID token condition reads the groups claim: members of the `administrator` group become Shopware administrators, members of the `editor` group get the `Editor` ACL role (products, categories, media and shopping experiences, privileges in `SHOPWARE_ACL_EDITOR_PRIVILEGES`). Every other rule of the Keycloak client is deleted. [`files/php/oidc/admins.php`](./files/php/oidc/admins.php) withdraws the admin flag from Keycloak-linked users outside the `administrator` group and the `Editor` ACL role from Keycloak-linked users outside the `editor` group, the platform administrator excepted; it runs as an RBAC hook of [sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync](../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/) at every deploy and on its timer."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Group-Based Admin Roles:** ```files/php/oidc/client.php`` <./files/php/oidc/client.php>`__ keeps two AdminOpenAuth role-assignment rules whose ID token condition reads the groups claim: members of the ``administrator`` group become Shopware administrators, members of the ``editor`` group get the ``Editor`` ACL role (products, categories, media and shopping experiences, privileges in ``SHOPWARE_ACL_EDITOR_PRIVILEGES``). Every other rule of the Keycloak client is deleted. ```files/php/oidc/admins.php`` <./files/php/oidc/admins.php>`__ withdraws the admin flag from Keycloak-linked users outside the ``administrator`` group and the ``Editor`` ACL role from Keycloak-linked users outside the ``editor`` group, the platform administrator excepted; it runs as an RBAC hook of `sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync <../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/>`__ at every deploy and on its timer."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Group-Based Teams and Roles:** [`files/php/seed/rbac.php`](./files/php/seed/rbac.php) keeps the teams `Users` and `Managers` with the roles `User` (team read, own edit, no delete) and `Manager` (every record), maps the `user` and `manager` role groups onto them through the groups claim (`oidcGroupClaim`, `oidcSyncTeams`, `oidcTeamsColumns`) and switches `aclStrictMode` on, so an account without a role group reaches no CRM record. It also sets the teams of existing accounts from the role-group members and makes the members of the `administrator` group EspoCRM administrators, every other account a regular user; the platform administrator, API and system users are never changed. It runs as an RBAC hook of [sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync](../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/) at every deploy and on its timer. With LDAP only, `ldapUserLoginFilter` admits only the members of the role groups."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Group-Based Teams and Roles:** ```files/php/seed/rbac.php`` <./files/php/seed/rbac.php>`__ keeps the teams ``Users`` and ``Managers`` with the roles ``User`` (team read, own edit, no delete) and ``Manager`` (every record), maps the ``user`` and ``manager`` role groups onto them through the groups claim (``oidcGroupClaim``, ``oidcSyncTeams``, ``oidcTeamsColumns``) and switches ``aclStrictMode`` on, so an account without a role group reaches no CRM record. It also sets the teams of existing accounts from the role-group members and makes the members of the ``administrator`` group EspoCRM administrators, every other account a regular user; the platform administrator, API and system users are never changed. It runs as an RBAC hook of `sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync <../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/>`__ at every deploy and on its timer. With LDAP only, ``ldapUserLoginFilter`` admits only the members of the role groups."
