msgid "**Read-only IdP fields:** ``services.sso.profile.locked`` decides which fields are locked. ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ renders its keys into ``WORDPRESS_OIDC_PROFILE_LOCKED``. On ``profile.php`` and ``user-edit.php`` of an OIDC account those fields are read-only with a translated warning as their hover title, rendered by the shared lock renderer of ``sys-front-inj-javascript``. Every write through ``wp_insert_user`` (the profile and user forms, ``/wp/v2/users``, XML-RPC ``wp.editProfile``, any plugin calling ``wp_update_user``) keeps their stored values, except the profile sync of the OIDC login itself. Removing a key unlocks its field in the form and on every write; the next OIDC login still overwrites it."
