msgid "An addon MAY pin a release through `config.archive`. Before `occ app:install`, [02_install.yml](./02_install.yml) stages the archive on the node and pipes it into [files/shell/utils/replace_pinned_app.sh](../../../files/shell/utils/replace_pinned_app.sh) inside the container:"
msgstr ""

msgid "An addon MAY set `config.background_install: true`. `recognize` sets it."
msgstr ""

msgid "An addon MUST NOT bridge a service that is absent from `meta/services.yml`; lint fails with the missing key named."
msgstr ""

msgid "An addon in ``meta/addons/<id>.yml`` declares the same fields in its ``update:`` block, beside ``monitored``, ``catalog`` and ``upstream_id``. A monitored addon of the ``github-releases`` catalog needs no ``type``: its ``upstream_id`` already names the repository whose tags are its versions. An addon's ``config.archive`` URL carries the pinned version and moves with it."
msgstr ""

msgid "An addon pins its version at the root of `meta/addons/<id>.yml` and declares the same fields in its `update:` block, beside `monitored`, `catalog` and `upstream_id`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "An addon resolves its tarball from `MEDIAWIKI_EXT_URL_PREFIX` plus its own id and the `REL<major>_<minor>` branch matching the pinned image. An addon that declares `config.archive` in `meta/addons/<id>.yml` uses that URL instead; `AWS` does, because Extension:AWS lives at `edwardspec/mediawiki-aws-s3` rather than under `wikimedia/mediawiki-extensions-*`, and the only `REL` branch it carries is `REL1_34`."
msgstr ""

msgid "An addon resolves its tarball from ``MEDIAWIKI_EXT_URL_PREFIX`` plus its own id and the ``REL<major>_<minor>`` branch matching the pinned image. An addon that declares ``config.archive`` in ``meta/addons/<id>.yml`` uses that URL instead; ``AWS`` does, because Extension:AWS lives at ``edwardspec/mediawiki-aws-s3`` rather than under ``wikimedia/mediawiki-extensions-*``, and the only ``REL`` branch it carries is ``REL1_34``."
msgstr ""

msgid "An addon that needs install/enable/configure logic beyond the generic `config:` payload MUST place it in `roles/<role>/tasks/addons/<addon_id>.yml`, mirroring the `meta/addons/<addon_id>.yml` file-root convention."
msgstr ""

msgid "An addon that stays in the tree while its partner is EOL gates on exactly `{{ lookup('config', '<own-role>', 'services.<eol-key>.enabled') | bool }}`, which the stored literal holds at `false`; the rule matches that expression anchored over the whole value, accepting either quote character and whitespace after `lookup(` and around its commas, because a gate that merely mentions the lookup can still render true. An addon reaching an external SaaS provider through `lookup('api_enabled', …)` declares no `bridges:` and is not a dependency on the in-repo role at all."
msgstr ""

msgid "An addon under `meta/addons/` MAY declare an `incompatible_plugins` list in its `config:`. The plan's `disable` list carries every listed plugin that ends up off and still runs, and [02_install.yml](./02_install.yml) disables the listed plugins again before an install attempt. This guarantees that mutually exclusive integrations such as the OIDC entry points (`oidc_login`, `sociallogin`, `user_oidc`) and the document-editing surfaces (`onlyoffice`, `richdocuments`, `fileslibreofficeedit`) cannot accidentally coexist on the same instance."
msgstr ""

