msgstr ""

msgid "An addon's `config.archive` stays a literal URL that carries the pinned version:"
msgstr ""

msgid "An address is matched before that, on the raw text, because a URL carries the characters the stripping removes."
msgstr ""

msgid "An agent is a role. A role has one soul with one `## Objective`, runs one or more skills, and each skill builds on zero or more routines. Work flows top down: a role runs skills, a skill builds on routines, a routine calls `cli/` and `utils/`. A routine never calls a skill, a skill never calls a role."
msgstr ""

msgid "An agent's `account` grants form an ordered list: the order of its `firewall_roles` binding, then the rule order inside each role, with inventory overrides able to reorder it."
msgstr ""

msgid "An agent's account grants form an ordered list. A grant is active only while its credentials are present (in the inventory or provisioned); an inactive grant is skipped. The first active grant is the default account, used by every routine step that needs an account and names none. When a grant goes inactive, the next active one becomes the default."
msgstr ""

msgid "An algorithm change (router parameters such as fall-through order, failure threshold and settle rule; an engine's declared capabilities such as `services.libretranslate-engine.serves`; masking; damage predicate; glossary; client settings) is opened only with a benchmark: a fixed evaluation set per language built from human-reviewed Weblate strings, scored by the chat judge before and after; it must improve at least one language and lower none."
msgstr ""

msgid "An answer about the item is ``OPEN`` or ``CLOSED``, and HTTP 404 or 410 is ``MISSING``. A timeout, a connection error, HTTP 429 and a 5xx answer are retried with a doubling pause before they count. An exhausted rate limit (a 429 that survives the retries, or a 403 that carries ``X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0`` or ``Retry-After``) is ``RATE_LIMITED``, with the reset time the tracker announced. Everything else that still fails is ``UNVERIFIED``: a network error, an auth wall, any other status, a body that is not a JSON object and a state the adapter does not know. A tracker that could not be asked therefore never reads as one that said the item is still open."
msgstr ""

msgid "An app that needs an extra mapper MUST add it through a per-client scope. See [nextcloud.json.j2](../../../../roles/web-app-keycloak/templates/import/scopes/nextcloud.json.j2) for the precedent: a dedicated scope holds the Nextcloud-specific UID and quota mappers and is attached only to the Nextcloud client."
msgstr ""

msgid "An app the background job has not checked yet is not updated until its next run."
