msgstr ""

msgid "The marker lives outside the stack and its volumes, so it survives ``docker stack rm``, ``docker compose down``, a crashed database and the stop and start cycle of ``backup.project_hard_restart``. A host that carries the marker therefore redeploys while its dedicated database is down, as in the restore of ```svc-bkp-nfs-2-local`` <../svc-bkp-nfs-2-local/README.md>`__ (``docker stack rm``, restore, redeploy). A dedicated store on a host without the marker, such as a 0.16 host or a host whose instance directory was lost, needs its database running before the deploy: start the database service of the stack the host last deployed, then deploy. Before a host that carries the marker goes back to a 0.16 store, through ``stalwart-migrate rollback`` or a backup taken under 0.16, delete the marker, so the next deploy reads the store."
msgstr ""

msgid "The marker lives outside the stack and its volumes, so it survives `docker stack rm`, `docker compose down`, a crashed database and the stop and start cycle of `backup.project_hard_restart`. A host that carries the marker therefore redeploys while its dedicated database is down, as in the restore of [`svc-bkp-nfs-2-local`](../svc-bkp-nfs-2-local/README.md) (`docker stack rm`, restore, redeploy). A dedicated store on a host without the marker, such as a 0.16 host or a host whose instance directory was lost, needs its database running before the deploy: start the database service of the stack the host last deployed, then deploy. Before a host that carries the marker goes back to a 0.16 store, through `stalwart-migrate rollback` or a backup taken under 0.16, delete the marker, so the next deploy reads the store."
