msgid "Weblate is served on clearnet over https and on its onion sibling over plain http, from one container. Upstream builds every absolute URL, including the OIDC ``redirect_uri``, from ``SITE_URL``. ```files/python/settings_override.py`` <files/python/settings_override.py>`__ is mounted at ``/app/data/settings-override.py``, the file upstream’s ``settings_docker.py`` execs last. It replaces ``weblate.middleware.ProxyMiddleware`` and ``weblate.accounts.strategy.WeblateStrategy`` with the subclasses in ```files/python/weblate_network/middleware.py`` <files/python/weblate_network/middleware.py>`__ and ```files/python/weblate_network/strategy.py`` <files/python/weblate_network/strategy.py>`__, mounted as the namespace package ``weblate_network`` under ``/app/infinito``, which take scheme and host from the request. They live in two modules because ``social_django.utils`` imports the strategy at app-ready time, before it defines the ``load_strategy`` that ``weblate.middleware`` imports back. The strategy module therefore imports nothing beyond ``weblate.accounts.strategy``. The host is validated against ``WEBLATE_ALLOWED_HOSTS``, which lists every network sibling, the internal service name and the loopback names. The override also turns off ``SECURE_SSL_REDIRECT`` and ``SOCIAL_AUTH_REDIRECT_IS_HTTPS``, because the proxy already redirects clearnet http to https. It sets the language cookie to ``SameSite=Lax``."
msgstr ""

msgid "Weblate is served on clearnet over https and on its onion sibling over plain http, from one container. Upstream builds every absolute URL, including the OIDC `redirect_uri`, from `SITE_URL`. [`files/python/settings_override.py`](files/python/settings_override.py) is mounted at `/app/data/settings-override.py`, the file upstream's `settings_docker.py` execs last. It replaces `weblate.middleware.ProxyMiddleware` and `weblate.accounts.strategy.WeblateStrategy` with the subclasses in [`files/python/weblate_network/middleware.py`](files/python/weblate_network/middleware.py) and [`files/python/weblate_network/strategy.py`](files/python/weblate_network/strategy.py), mounted as the namespace package `weblate_network` under `/app/infinito`, which take scheme and host from the request. They live in two modules because `social_django.utils` imports the strategy at app-ready time, before it defines the `load_strategy` that `weblate.middleware` imports back. The strategy module therefore imports nothing beyond `weblate.accounts.strategy`. The host is validated against `WEBLATE_ALLOWED_HOSTS`, which lists every network sibling, the internal service name and the loopback names. The override also turns off `SECURE_SSL_REDIRECT` and `SOCIAL_AUTH_REDIRECT_IS_HTTPS`, because the proxy already redirects clearnet http to https. It sets the language cookie to `SameSite=Lax`."
