msgid "When `/mnt` has at least `MIN_FREE_GB` free and more than `/`, [relocate_docker_dataroot.sh](../../../../../scripts/github/runner/relocate_docker_dataroot.sh) stops Docker and containerd, bind-mounts `/mnt/containerd` over `/var/lib/containerd` (images, container layers, the swarm node containers), sets the Docker data-root to `/mnt/docker-host` (named volumes), restarts both and verifies that containerd's metadata and the Docker root sit on `/mnt`. Before the stop it fails if Docker already holds containers, images, volumes or build cache, if another containerd namespace holds containers or tasks, if containerd shims run, or if `daemon.json` cannot be read as JSON. Any failure after the stop, and a cancel, unmounts the bind, restores `daemon.json`, restarts both daemons and fails the step. It refuses under act and changes nothing on a runner that is not GitHub-hosted. Every decline prints a `::notice::` annotation and no runner-state dump, because a decline changes nothing: the swap step right after it dumps that same state. A successful relocation dumps the new state. [run.py](../../../../../utils/tests/swarm/run.py) then watches the free space of both `/` and `/var/lib/containerd`."
