msgid "[ ] hacker: credential brute forcing runs only against seeded test accounts, stays under the lockout threshold, stops at the first proof, and locks no account out of service (fixture with a seeded weak test credential and a seeded throttle)."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] hacker: every failed check and a failed scan run send an email to the security contact that carries only severity and link."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] hacker: every seeded finding of the fixture app becomes a work package in the confidential security project with severity, affected role and reproduction steps, and without live secrets."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] hacker: no scan sends more requests per second than its configured rate limit."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] hacker: the analysers report the fixture app's seeded weaknesses (vulnerable dependency, missing security header, weak TLS) as findings (one fixture per analyser)."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] hacker: without `agents.hacker.targets` the hacker does not start; a production run waits for the owner's approval of that run."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] npm installs succeed inside the sandbox."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] operator: a backup restore waits for the owner's approval."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] operator: a seeded alarm (full disk, expiring certificate, failed backup) starts its runbook routine and ends as a work package with timeline and cause."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] planner: a second issue with the same content is linked to the existing work package instead of creating a new one."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] planner: an issue becomes a `Proposed` work package with user story and checkable criteria, linked to the issue."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] port-ui carries no RBAC or health logic and no configuration for them."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] release: a green default branch produces a release draft with notes; the tag waits for approval."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] reviewer: a pull request whose new spec has no negative control gets `changes requested`. Partly met: the routine routes a changed spec without a passing control to `changes requested` (`tests/unit/python/agents/routines/test_reviewer.py`); posting the verdict is not wired yet."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] reviewer: an agent pull request with a missing evidence comment gets `changes requested`; a clean one gets `recommend merge`; the reviewer never reviews its own pull request. Partly met: the routine decides all three (`agents/routines/reviewer.py`, `agents/routines/tools/review_checklist.py`, `tests/unit/python/agents/routines/test_reviewer.py`); posting the verdict on the forge from the deployed orchestrator is not wired yet."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] security: a seeded CVE feed entry for a pinned image produces one work package per affected role with the advisory id, the affected and the fixed version, and, where the fix is a public bump, a GitHub issue handed to the maintainer (fixture feed)."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] security: a seeded vulnerable dependency becomes a work package in the confidential security project."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] security: the deployed-component inventory and the hardening floor are built from registry and manifest metadata with no image pull and no request to a running instance (probe recorded)."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] support: a defect described in a ticket becomes a `Proposed` work package linked to the ticket."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] support: a draft never contains a secret, an internal hostname or another customer's data (fixture test)."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] support: a new Zammad ticket gets a drafted answer with cited sources as internal note, drawn only from public docs, role READMEs and approved answers with customer data removed."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] support: the answer reaches the customer only after the owner approves it; a rejection with a remark produces a revised draft."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] support: the approval view shows the full outgoing text and every attachment."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] tester: a coverage gap between `meta/services.yml` and the specs becomes a pull request with the missing spec."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] tester: a seeded spec that cannot fail is detected by its negative control and hardened in a pull request."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: `make i18n-pause` pauses the tools lane container and `make i18n-resume` continues it with its models and connections intact; no request leaves the lane while it is paused (probe recorded)."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: a language whose catalog fails verification (empty or fuzzy entry, `msgfmt --check` error, changed placeholder or protected span, lost glossary term) gets no pull request and is reported (one fixture per failure kind)."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: a language whose sampled chat-judge level falls below its last accepted level gets no pull request, and a judge reply without a level aborts that language's verification."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: a merge that adds translatable strings is queued, and the cron start at 23:00 UTC runs `i18n-extract`, `i18n-prune`, `i18n-translate` and `i18n-retry` without a human running them."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: after `agents.translator.max_attempts` failed attempts an entry is no longer retried, stays marked for a human, and is listed in the translator's report (fixture of a string every engine fails)."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: an algorithm pull request carries the benchmark table per language, and a change that lowers any language's score is discarded (fixture)."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: an entry that fails the separate `make test-oracle` judgement is retranslated in the next window with the engine that produced it excluded."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: at 23:00 UTC the night cron starts or resumes translation regardless of load, and at 07:00 UTC it pauses it and hands over to the day rule (fixture clock). Partly met: `agents/roles/translator/cron.yml` carries the start and pause entries of both windows and `utils/orchestrator/load.py` lets a pause outrank a start of the same tick (`tests/unit/python/utils/orchestrator/test_load.py`); the orchestrator scheduler does not pass measured conditions to `cron.due` and does not act on the result yet."
msgstr ""

#, no-python-format
msgid "[ ] translator: during the day, a tick with CPU and GPU below 30 % starts or resumes translation, and a tick with CPU or GPU above 95 % pauses it (fixture load figures). Partly met: as above, `conditions` in `utils/orchestrator/load.py`; the load sampling in the orchestrator is missing."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: each language gets its own pull request with only that language's catalogs, and no language pull request contains algorithm changes."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: new strings get machine translations through `web-svc-translate` as Weblate suggestions, and a human-reviewed string stays unchanged."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: on a host where `accelerated()` is false, the GPU condition counts as met. Partly met: `conditions(..., accelerated=False)` in `utils/orchestrator/load.py`; the orchestrator does not read `accelerated()` yet."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: the day rule ignores the translation lane's own load, so a running translation at high own load with an idle rest of the system is not paused (fixture). Partly met: `rest_of_system` in `utils/orchestrator/load.py` with its red fixture; the per-container lane sample is missing."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: the evaluation set of each language is built from human-reviewed Weblate strings and is not used as translation input."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: the judge pass of a full night stays within its budget of about one hour of the window, measured on the host (recorded duration)."
msgstr ""

msgid "[ ] translator: the language set equals `domain_languages()` for each domain, only languages with changed catalogs get a pull request, and a language without a docs catalog gets it created in its first pull request."
msgstr ""

