msgid "`make cache-evict` first checks the disk floor `INFINITO_CACHE_DISK_FLOOR` (default `15g`): the caps fit the machine only when `free + used - sum(caps)` reaches it. Otherwise it exits non-zero before it evicts anything and names every cap variable. It then sweeps the shared folders and the models and evicts the Nexus blob store through its REST API, and prints one status line per cache. Its first run on a cache above its cap is the migration: the same age and size eviction, so entries accessed inside the idle window stay as far as the cap allows and no cache directory is removed or recreated. `make clean-cache` keeps its wipe semantics and is called by no other target."
