msgid "`tasks/01_admin.yml` realigns the declared administrator password on every deploy, so `INITIAL_ADMIN_PW` is only still needed for the very first installation. The backend image hands it to `kix.Console.pl Admin::User::SetPassword admin` as a command argument (`/usr/local/bin/docker-entrypoint.sh` line 194), so the value is part of the process argument list inside the backend container while that installation runs. Cause: upstream entrypoint, the console command `Admin::User::SetPassword` takes the password as an argument only. Options: find out what `install_kix()` stores when `INITIAL_ADMIN_PW` is unset and drop the variable from `templates/env.j2` if the realign covers it; or report it upstream."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/01_administrator.yml` lines 24 and 42 pass `DJANGO_SUPERUSER_PASSWORD={{ TAIGA_SUPERUSER_PASSWORD | quote }}` as an argument of `container exec`, so a deploy at `-vv` with `MASK_CREDENTIALS_IN_LOGS` off prints the administrator password in the task's `cmd`. Options: forward it as `-e DJANGO_SUPERUSER_PASSWORD` without a value plus the task's `environment:`, or pipe the shell snippet on stdin."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/01_init.yml`: **per-consumer provisioning** (create the ACL user / vhost / namespace and its credentials), idempotent, mirroring postgres `01_init`."
